    "steps": [
        {
            "implementation details": "I. Cox Proportional Hazards Models: The authors utilized Cox proportional hazards regression models to evaluate the association between the circuit activity values derived from mechanistic models and overall patient survival in sarcoma samples. The model includes covariates such as tissue categories (sarcoma subtypes and normal tissues) and the tissue source site to correct for batch effects. The coxph function from the survival R package was employed for model fitting. The proportional hazards assumption was tested using the cox.zph function, ensuring that the hazard ratios remain consistent over time.",
            "original text": "Survival analysis was performed on sarcoma samples using the survival R package [50] version 3.2\u201310. From this package, Cox proportional hazards regression models [51] were computed to estimate differences in patient survival in association with circuit activity or gene expression values."
