            "implementation details": "III. Hazard Ratio Calculation: The hazard ratios for the identified circuits were calculated using the coxph function to assess their impact on survival. The p-values for each circuit's hazard ratio were adjusted for multiple comparisons using the Benjamini and Hochberg method to control for false discovery rate. Additional survival analysis of circuit-integrating genes was conducted using external tools such as KMplot and UALCAN to validate the findings and assess their relevance across different cancer types.",
            "original text": "The activation of signaling pathways is closely related to cell fate and may have a causal influence on patient survival. Here, the association of the modeled circuit activity values with sarcoma patients\u2019 overall survival was explored in detail. To achieve this, Cox proportional hazard models and Kaplan\u2013Meier plots were employed."
        }
    ]
}

